cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this certificate or verifier, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Exact certificate excluding seven mutually unbiased bases in C^6 without Fourier vanishing (verifier and data)"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: 2026-11-17
repository-code: "https://github.com/OIerYangJZ/mub6-vanishing-free-certificate"
authors:
  - family-names: "Yang"
    given-names: "Jinze"
    affiliation: "School of Physics, Xidian University"
abstract: >-
  Standalone exact verifier (Python standard library only; integer and rational arithmetic)
  and certificate data proving that there are no seven mutually unbiased bases in C^6, hence
  N(6) <= 5 by Weiner's gap theorem. The certificate reuses the six test-function lists of
  OpenAI's mixed-moment certificate but never uses the Fourier-vanishing input (their
  eq. (27)), the single-matrix identity (10), or the cubic exclusion (Prop. 5.2). New positive
  definite integer Gram matrices give f + sum|beta| = -201252715232209/9720 < 0.
keywords:
  - mutually unbiased bases
  - complex Hadamard matrices
  - dimension six
  - computer-assisted proof
  - exact certificate
  - positive semidefinite certificate
references:
